language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Find positive integers a and b such that a - b is a prime number p and a * b is a perfect square n * n, with a at least min_a; minimise a.
given min_a : int(1..)
given max_val : int(1..)
find a : int(1..max_val)
find b : int(1..max_val)
find n : int(1..max_val)
find p : int(2..max_val)

minimising a

such that
$ a is no less than the given minimum
a >= min_a,
$ b is a positive integer
b >= 1,
$ a - b is the prime number p
a - b = p,
$ p is prime: no k from 2 to p-1 divides p
forAll k : int(2..max_val) . ((k < p) -> (p % k != 0)),
$ a times b is the perfect square n * n
a * b = n * n
